# BaluHost — grant the service user write access to AMD GPU sysfs power
# control nodes so the GPU power manager can apply performance levels and
# profile modes without needing root.
#
# Background: AMDGPU exposes power control via two sysfs files:
#   /sys/class/drm/card*/device/power_dpm_force_performance_level
#   /sys/class/drm/card*/device/pp_power_profile_mode
# Both are owned root:root with mode 0644 by default. A systemd service
# running as ${BALUHOST_USER} therefore hits PermissionError ([Errno 13])
# when the GPU power manager tries to switch states.
#
# #516: the same problem applies to the four GPU fan acoustics nodes under
# gpu_od/fan_ctrl/ (fan target temperature, acoustic limit/target RPM
# thresholds, minimum PWM). gpu_od/ only exists once the amdgpu driver has
# initialized Overdrive for that card — on a card where Overdrive is off or
# unsupported, the directory is simply absent. The `[ -e ]` guard below
# already covers that: the loop skips missing files instead of failing, so
# adding these paths is safe even on hardware without gpu_od/. Whether the
# rule really fires for them can therefore only be established after a boot
# on which gpu_od/ exists — and it has to be measured on the permissions
# themselves:
#
#   ls -la /sys/class/drm/card0/device/gpu_od/fan_ctrl/
#   # expected: root video, group-write set
#
# Checking that the acoustics feature works proves nothing here: the backend
# falls back to `sudo -n tee`, and the hardware sudoers template lists these
# four nodes by name (narrowed from a /sys/class/hwmon/* wildcard in #570), so
# the values take effect even while these nodes are still root:root 0644.
#
# This udev rule re-chowns the relevant sysfs nodes to the "video" group
# and adds the group-write bit. ${BALUHOST_USER} must be a member of
# "video" — the install script ensures this via `usermod -aG video`.
#
# Re-runs on every boot (and on hot card add / suspend resume), so the
# permissions stay correct across reboots.
#
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", \
    RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'for f in /sys/class/drm/%k/device/power_dpm_force_performance_level /sys/class/drm/%k/device/pp_power_profile_mode /sys/class/drm/%k/device/gpu_od/fan_ctrl/fan_target_temperature /sys/class/drm/%k/device/gpu_od/fan_ctrl/acoustic_limit_rpm_threshold /sys/class/drm/%k/device/gpu_od/fan_ctrl/acoustic_target_rpm_threshold /sys/class/drm/%k/device/gpu_od/fan_ctrl/fan_minimum_pwm; do [ -e \"$f\" ] && chgrp video \"$f\" && chmod g+w \"$f\"; done'"
